      { question: "Can a GaN charger damage my laptop by delivering too much power?", answer: "No. USB-PD negotiation is device-driven — the laptop requests a specific voltage and current, and the charger delivers only what was asked. A properly certified charger cannot push more power than the device negotiates." },
